Cell["Introduction", "IntroductionSection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This notebook contains the code to generate the graphics from the \
Functions website (",
  ButtonBox["functions.wolfram.com",
    ButtonData:>{
      URL[ "http://functions.wolfram.com"], None},
    ButtonStyle->"Hyperlink"],
  ") for the function ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{"W", "(", "z", ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ".\n\nThe code in this notebook is tailored to generate the graphics shown \
on the website using ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " 5. No claim of correctness and generality, responsibility for proper \
performance, or support in any form is given. \n\nWith sufficient memory and \
CPU power, the notebook can be evaluated at once from beginning to end.\n\n\
This notebook also generates a number of intermediate graphics needed to \
assemble the final graphics shown on the website.\n\nAll graphics from this \
notebook are copyrighted. For permission to use them, send email to ",
  ButtonBox["permissions@wolfram.com",
    ButtonData:>{
      URL[ "mailto:permission@wolfram.com"], None},
    ButtonStyle->"Hyperlink"],
  ".\n\nFor comments on any of the graphics, send email to ",
  ButtonBox["comments@functions.wolfram.com",
    ButtonData:>{
      URL[ "mailto:comments@functions.wolfram.com"], None},
    ButtonStyle->"Hyperlink"],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell["This notebook was last updated 16-07-2003.", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The purpose of the code presented here is to generate visualizations. To \
avoid large function values and numerical instabilities, the code frequently \
starts at a value that is a small distance away from singularities and \
discontinuities (typically between ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["10", 
          RowBox[{"-", "6"}]], TraditionalForm]]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["10", 
          RowBox[{"-", "12"}]], TraditionalForm]]],
  ") .\nAs a rule, red curves are for the real part, blue curves for the \
imaginary part, violet curves for absolute values, and green curves for \
arguments. If not stated otherwise, surfaces are colored for aesthetic \
reasons."
}], "Text"]
}, Closed]],

